Key Market Drivers
1. Infrastructure Rehabilitation Demands
The global market is experiencing accelerated growth due to aging transportation infrastructure, with governments allocating record budgets for road and bridge maintenance. In the U.S. alone, the Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act has earmarked $110 billion for roads and bridges, creating substantial demand for high-performance resurfacing materials. This trend is mirrored globally, with the market growing approximately 7.8% annually over the past five years.

2. Residential Renovation Boom
Homeowners increasingly prefer resurfacing over replacement for outdoor concrete surfaces. The residential segment now accounts for 42% of total market revenue, driven by:

Significant cost advantages versus full replacement
Expanding DIY home improvement trends
Growing popularity of decorative concrete finishes
➤ The global decorative concrete market (including resurfacing products) is projected to reach $19.2 billion by 2028

Market Challenges
While the market shows strong growth potential, several challenges require attention:

Skilled Labor Shortages - Proper application requires certified contractors, with improper installations accounting for 18% of industry complaints
Weather Sensitivity - Temperature and humidity constraints reduce viable installation windows by 30-45 days annually in temperate regions
Material Cost Volatility - Epoxy resin prices have fluctuated 18-22% annually since 2021, squeezing manufacturer margins
